    <!-- One paragraph per item, in order - see PrivacyPolicyPage() in SetupPageContent.kt. -->
    <string-array name="privacy_page">
        <item>Privacy Policy\nEffective Date: July 21, 2026</item>
        <item>Shuttle Tracker (“the App”) respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle your information.</item>
        <item>Information We Collect\nThe App may access your device location in order to:</item>
        <item>Show you the closest shuttle stop.\nCalculate how far you are from that stop.</item>
        <item>We do not collect, store, or transmit your location data or any other personal information. All processing happens locally on your device.</item>
        <item>Use of Information\nLocation data is used only in real time to display shuttle stop information.</item>
        <item>Your location data is never stored, logged, or sent to our servers.</item>
        <item>Push Notifications\nThe App uses Firebase Cloud Messaging to deliver optional service announcements. This assigns your device a registration token, which is sent to Firebase’s servers so we can deliver notifications to it. We do not attach any other personal information to this token, and you can decline or disable notifications at any time without losing any other functionality of the App.</item>
        <item>Sharing of Information\nWe do not share your location or any other personal information with third parties, beyond what is necessary for Firebase Cloud Messaging (operated by Google) to deliver push notifications as described above.</item>
        <item>Children’s Privacy\nShuttle Tracker does not knowingly collect, store, or share personal information from children.</item>
        <item>Changes to This Policy\nIf we make changes to this Privacy Policy, we will update it here and revise the “Effective Date” above.</item>
        <item>Contact Us\nIf you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, you can contact us at:\nBryan Tran\nbryan.tran0205@gmail.com</item>
        <item>Joel McCandless\nmail@joelmccandless.com</item>
    </string-array>

    <string name="about_page">Shuttle Tracker is developed by the Rensselaer Center for Open Source
        by your fellow RPI students. As an open source application, anyone can help develop the RPI Shuttle Tracker
        regardless of experience! Any contributions are welcome, as well as feedback for our current team.
        If you would like to view our source code, click the button below and open our GitHub page, and you can
        open an \"issue\" to leave feedback for us. View our privacy policy with the button below.</string>

